export anchor VaultStyle:
    number: 368
    screen: FinanceBudget
    name: Vault
    idea: The money app as a steel vault, riveted brushed steel plates, numbered deposit boxes with keyholes and inset readouts for balances, a combination dial for the savings goal and drawer fronts with gauges and indicator lamps for the budget.
    base: dark
    palette:
        floor: #121417, the page and the style sheet
        steel: #2a2f35, riveted plates, drawers and the dial face
        steelLow: #22262b, sheet heading plates and the dial hub
        edge: #4a525c, plate edges, rivet rims and bevels
        inset: #0b0d0f, readouts, the log, gauges, fields and stamps
        ink: #e3e7ea, text, readout figures and major dial ticks
        etched: #a9b2bb, labels, box numbers, minor ticks and gauge fill
        amber: #ffb84d, the dial arc and pointer, the Sealed lamp, the primary button and focus
        greenLamp: #8fe0a0, drawers with money left and deposits
        redLamp: #ff8c7a, the over limit drawer and the owed balance
    type:
        Labels use Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow,
        system-ui in caps. Readouts use ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas. The plate
        title is 20px at 700 tracked .24em with an embossed text shadow. Box
        readouts are 22px mono, box labels 15px at 700 tracked .12em, the log
        13px mono and section labels 12px tracked .22em.
    layout:
        A 1200px vault. A riveted header plate holds Brightwork Money, Vault, a
        caps line for Mara Okafor, October, EUR, and four inset nav keys,
        Overview outlined in amber. Then three columns, 300px, flexible and
        320px. Deposit boxes stacks three riveted plates, BOX 01 to BOX 03, each
        with a round keyhole and a pressed in dark readout, the card readout in
        red with a clock and Owed, due 12 Nov. The Goal dial plate has Japan
        trip over a large combination dial with 100 ticks, numbers every ten, an
        amber arc to 64, a pointer at 64 and 64 PERCENT in the hub, and a three
        cell inset readout for 3,200 saved, 5,000 target and Open by 1 Apr 27.
        The Access log plate holds an inset list with date, payee, a DEPOSIT or
        WITHDRAWAL tag with an arrow and amount. A wide Budget drawers plate
        follows with five drawer fronts, each with a name, a lamp, a pull
        handle, a segmented inset gauge, spent over limit and a stamped word.
        Totals sit under the drawers. Below 1100px the dial goes first and full
        width. Below 680px everything stacks and drawers go two across.
    spacing:
        A 4px unit. 20px between plates, 14px between boxes, 12px between
        drawers, 20 to 28px plate padding.
    density: Medium. Three boxes, one big dial, a five line log and five drawers.
    corners:
        6px plates, 4px drawers, buttons and readouts, with round rivets,
        keyholes and swatches.
    borders:
        1px steel edge on every plate with a light top bevel and a dark bottom
        bevel. Insets have no border, only an inner shadow.
    shadows:
        Heavy. Plates cast 0 6px 14px black, drawers and buttons sit on a hard
        3px dark ledge and readouts are pressed in.
    icons:
        Hardware as icons, rivets, keyholes, handles and lamps. The lamp shape
        changes with state, a round green lamp for money left, a square amber
        lamp for Sealed and a red triangle for Over 62, each beside a stamped
        word with a circle check, ruled square or triangle.
    focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
    tone:
        Vault words in caps, such as Deposit boxes, Goal dial, Access log,
        Sealed, Over 62 and Open by.
